From 3c4fae931ac4b77ef226d0703fee1ff5344317f9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chiro <chiro2001@163.com>
Date: Sat, 12 Sep 2026 08:55:18 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 224/256] test(cpu): pin SVE256 W8A8 artifact memo discipline

Six focused assertions for the W8A8 decode memo:

- repeated `_load_w8a8` calls decode once and share the same
  LoadedSve256Artifact (identity keyed, not metadata-blind);
- a 2-node W8A8 launch (qmatmul + epilogue) performs exactly one
  `_decode_for_execution` (4 before the fix: 1 launch + qmatmul 1 +
  epilogue double decode);
- `PYPTO_X_SVE_W8A8_DECODE_MEMO=off` restores one full decode per
  dispatch and leaves the memo empty (A/B reproduction switch);
- the memo is bounded to its 2-entry limit with FIFO eviction;
- a fresh Artifact object over a 1-byte-tampered ELF misses the memo,
  is rejected fail-closed by the full decode and leaves the warmed
  entry usable;
- `_require_w8a8_declaration` still runs on every dispatch, including
  memo hits (a rejecting gate propagates), and a new Artifact with a
  tampered `w8a8_capability.digest` is rejected as well.
